# libpdx-pds-parser -- caps.decl
#
# Waves:
#   R221 (parser-tier Unicode + lexer umbrella, paideia-os#2485)
#   R222 (cmd-functor umbrella, paideia-os#2486)
#   R223 (pipeline-lang umbrella, paideia-os#2487)
#   R224 (lambda-lang umbrella, paideia-os#2488)
#   R225 (typechecker umbrella, paideia-os#2489)
#   R226 (datalog umbrella, paideia-os#2490)
#   R229 (REPL evaluator umbrella, paideia-os#2493)
# libpdx-pds-parser is a USER-SPACE shared library providing
# parser-tier wrappers over the kernel-side libpdx-unicode-tables
# substrate (R131). Every entry point is a pure leaf (or a leaf that
# delegates to libpdx-unicode-tables) over caller-supplied raw
# pointers.
#
# This file therefore declares the ABSENCE of required capabilities
# at the ENTRY-POINT floor -- a downstream tool linking this library
# does not need to grant anything beyond its own data-buffer read /
# write capability. Every primitive here is `effects: {mem},
# capabilities: {}` or `effects: {}, capabilities: {}` (lib.pdx's
# feature-level accessor is pure).
#
# consumed_kinds: none through all currently-planned M-landings.
#
#   R221.M1 UTF-8 decoder + NFC normalizer: calls into libpdx-
#      unicode-tables's _norm_nfc (R131.M3) via linker-resolved
#      symbol; no KIND surface.
#   R221.M2 grapheme cluster iterator: calls into libpdx-unicode-
#      tables's _gc_next (R131.M2) via linker-resolved symbol; no
#      KIND.
#   R221.M3 width pass (width_pass.pdx, landed): parser-tier TR#11
#      column classifier + cluster-aware column accumulator.
#      `_wp_char_width` delegates to libpdx-unicode-tables's
#      `_width_char` (R131.M5) for the primary classification and
#      overlays an 18-range A-class table from parser-tier .rodata
#      iff `_wp_locale_amb_state == 1` (East-Asian locale asked for
#      Ambiguous==2). `_wp_cluster_width` calls `utf8_decode_cp`
#      (R131.M1) + `_wp_char_width`. `_wp_cols` walks via
#      `_gi_next_cluster` (R221.M2, intra-library) + `utf8_decode_cp`
#      (R131.M1) + `_wp_char_width`. `_wp_locale_amb_width` /
#      `_wp_set_locale_amb` are pure-leaf .bss accessors. No KIND;
#      no new ambient capability.
#   R221.M4 context-tracking lexer (ctx_lexer.pdx, landed): pure
#      byte-walker over this library's M1 NFC-normalised output
#      buffer that captures pipeline / datalog / lambda tier
#      membership once at lex time. `_cl_init` is a pure-leaf boot
#      hook that zero-fills the module's three .bss singletons
#      (_cl_stack 16 B, _cl_depth u64, _cl_last_kind u64). The
#      three stack primitives (`_cl_push_ctx`, `_cl_pop_ctx`,
#      `_cl_current_ctx`) are pure-leaf accessors over the stack.
#      `_cl_lex_token` is a pure leaf (no nested CALL) that walks
#      bytes to the next token boundary and emits a 16-byte Token
#      record (kind u16, ctx u8, flags u8, src_offset u32,
#      src_length u32, payload u32). Stack mutations on `{` (push
#      BEFORE emit) and `}` (emit THEN pop) are inlined via direct
#      .bss writes. `_cl_tokenize` has ONE nested CALL per
#      iteration into `_cl_lex_token`; frame is 5 pushes + sub rsp,16
#      (two local slots cursor_in + tok_count) giving rsp%16==0 at
#      the nested CALL. No KIND; no external cross-library
#      dependency; no intra-library dependency at M4 (the lexer is
#      fully self-contained and uses only its own .bss state and
#      the caller-supplied input / output buffers; R221.M5 unified-
#      AST landing will add an intra-library consumer that READS
#      Token records). Treats every emitted token as a byte-span
#      reference into the caller's buffer -- the lexer never
#      allocates and never copies bytes outside the caller's out
#      buffer.
#   R221.M5 unified AST (ast.pdx, landed): singleton 8 KiB bump-
#      pointer node pool (256 x 32-byte SyntaxNode slots) in this
#      library's own .bss. Seven public entry points: `_ast_init`
#      (hard-reset of three scalar .bss singletons -- pool_next,
#      src_ptr, src_len), `_ast_set_source` (stash caller-supplied
#      source-byte pointer + length for the span-copy render), `_ast_
#      alloc(kind, src_offset, src_length)` (bump-allocate one 32-byte
#      slot and populate kind + Q-A5 span fields; pool_idx 0 reserved
#      as nil sentinel; returns 0 on pool-full), `_ast_set_payload_u32`
#      / `_ast_set_child_ref` / `_ast_set_extra_ref` (overwrite one
#      slot of an already-allocated node; silent no-op on bad ref),
#      `_ast_render` (span-copy the N bytes at _ast_src_ptr +
#      src_offset into the caller's out buffer; returns packed_u64).
#      All seven are PURE LEAVES -- zero callee-save pushes, zero
#      stack frames, zero nested CALLs; the allocator inlines the
#      lazy-init (precedent: `_rt_alloc_node` in row_types.pdx). No
#      KIND; no external module dependency; no intra-library module
#      dependency at M5 (the AST is a self-contained arena the
#      parser-tier downstream fills from CtxLexer R221.M4 Token
#      records). SyntaxKind enum spans five families on kilo-step
#      boundaries (0x0100 pipeline, 0x0200 datalog, 0x0300 lambda,
#      0x0400 record, 0x0500 literal) so a downstream dispatcher
#      discriminates via `shr r, 8; cmp r, imm8`. Error band
#      0x4400..0x44FF.
#   R221.M6 SpanMap (span_map.pdx, landed): source-span tracking
#      across UTF-8 -> NFC normalization. Preserves the Q-A5
#      invariant that every AST node points back into the ORIGINAL
#      caller-supplied source bytes, not the NFC-normalised output.
#      Four public entry points: `_sm_init` (hard-reset of
#      `_sm_pair_count` scalar; `.bss` zero-init at boot already
#      satisfies the cold-start identity-map state), `_sm_record_pair
#      (nfc_offset, src_offset)` (append one monotonic pair, enforcing
#      strict monotonicity across both offsets; pool cap 1024 at
#      8 B/stride for 8 KiB total `.bss`), `_sm_lookup(nfc_offset)`
#      (binary-search the pair array for the largest preceding
#      pair, return `pair.src + (nfc_offset - pair.nfc)` or identity
#      on empty-table), `_sm_from_u8nfc(bytes_src, src_len, bytes_nfc,
#      nfc_len)` (rebuild the span map in one pass by walking both
#      buffers in lockstep; records one pair per NFC composition
#      boundary; resync heuristic documented in design doc). Three
#      entry points (`_sm_init`, `_sm_record_pair`, `_sm_lookup`) are
#      PURE LEAVES; `_sm_from_u8nfc` has a 5-push + 16 B frame giving
#      rsp%16==0 at the two nested CALLs (`_sm_init`,
#      `_sm_record_pair`). No KIND; no external cross-library
#      dependency; no intra-library linker-visible dependency at raw
#      M6 (R221.M5 Ast stores span fields as u32; a future M6.1 AST
#      wire-up will call `_sm_lookup` from `_ast_render` to refine
#      the pre-NFC offset before span-copying). Error band
#      0x4700..0x47FF (4 slots used: SM_OK (0), SM_ERR_POOL_FULL
#      (0x4700), SM_ERR_NON_MONOTONIC (0x4701), SM_ERR_OOB_OFFSET
#      (0x4702, reserved), SM_ERR_BAD_INPUT (0x4703)).
#   R221.M7 fuzz corpus: tests only; no library-time surface.
#   R223.M1 Pipeline stage parser: pure in-process byte-walker +
#      records emitter over the caller's NFC-normalised input and
#      caller-supplied out buffer. Internally CALLs the
#      module-private _pl_emit_word helper. No KIND; no external
#      module dependency.
#   R223.M2 Record projection parser (record_projection.pdx):
#      pure in-process byte-walker + FieldSelector emitter over the
#      caller-supplied argv bytes (the argv of a `select` or
#      `project` pipeline stage, as located inside R223.M1's
#      PipelineStage records). _rp_parse_select / _rp_parse_project
#      are 1-nested-call wrappers that delegate to the module-
#      private _rp_parse_impl (which CALLs the module-private
#      _rp_skip_ws leaf). No KIND; no external module dependency.
#   R223.M3+ pipeline-lang follow-ups: no KIND surface planned;
#      consumers of this library (R222 cmd-functor dispatch,
#      R129.M5 renderer-override post-pass) remain the KIND-
#      touching tier.
#   R222.M1 SchemasSig parser (schemas_sig.pdx): pure in-process
#      byte-walker + field-descriptor emitter over the caller's
#      NFC-normalised input and caller-supplied out buffer.
#      _ss_parse_body CALLs the module-private _sch_sig_skip_ws +
#      _sch_sig_classify_type leaves; _ss_match_record is a M1 stub
#      (returns SS_UNIMPLEMENTED). No KIND; no external module
#      dependency.
#   R222.M2 CommandSig parser (command_sig.pdx): pure in-process
#      byte-walker + header + CapDecl emitter over the caller's
#      NFC-normalised input and caller-supplied out buffer.
#      _cs_parse_body CALLs the module-private _cmd_sig_skip_ws +
#      _cmd_sig_fnv1a64 leaves. No KIND; no external module
#      dependency. The cap-name identity hash is FNV-1a 64 (not
#      BLAKE3), chosen to keep this library pure-leaf; a later
#      R222.M? landing may swap it for a wrapper call to
#      paideia_crypto_blake3_hash without an ABI break (name_hash
#      slot stays u64).
#   R222.M4 ArgFlagSpec parser (arg_flag_spec.pdx): pure in-process
#      byte-walker + ArgSpec/FlagSpec emitter + invocation checker.
#      _afs_parse_arg_spec_body / _afs_parse_flag_spec_body CALL the
#      module-private _afs_skip_ws + _afs_classify_type leaves to
#      emit 32-byte ArgSpec / FlagSpec records; _afs_check_invocation
#      walks a FunctorInstance materialization record (R222.M3) and
#      CALLs _afs_parse_as_type for each positional / TAKES_VALUE
#      flag byte-run. No KIND; no external module dependency; no
#      cross-library dependency.
#   R222.M3+ cmd-functor follow-ups: REPL dispatch (M3) consumes
#      the CommandSig record + replaces R222.M1's _ss_match_record
#      stub with a full field-by-field type-code compare. ArgSpec /
#      FlagSpec (M4, landed) and the registry client (M5, landed)
#      layer over the same (header + descriptor array) byte image.
#      Still no KIND surface in this library -- the enclosing shell
#      session is where cap handles reify against the KIND-touching tier.
#   R222.M5 CmdRegistry client (cmd_registry.pdx): pure in-process
#      hash-table over caller-interned (name_hash, cs_body_ref,
#      functor_ref, scope) tuples. 128-slot .bss table, 48-byte
#      stride, closed addressing with linear probe. `_cmdreg_init`
#      zero-fills the table and resets the per-scope cursors
#      (idempotent lazy boot). `_cmdreg_register` CALLs
#      `_cmdreg_init` + `_cmdreg_fnv1a64` (both module-private
#      leaves) and claims the first unoccupied slot on the probe
#      chain. `_cmdreg_lookup` CALLs `_cmdreg_init` + `_cmdreg_fnv1a64`
#      and walks the probe chain, preferring SCOPE_USER (1) over
#      SCOPE_SYSTEM (0) on a name_hash tie. `_cmdreg_dump` CALLs
#      `_cmdreg_init` and copies all occupied entries into a caller
#      buffer for the `describe` command. No KIND; no external
#      module dependency; no cross-library dependency; at M5 the
#      TOML parser lives in R123.M2 kernel-side cmd_registry_parser.pdx
#      and this user-space client reads a pre-flattened byte buffer
#      (the kernel-side TOML parse chains in at R222.M6).
#   R222.M6 DispatchMode (dispatch_mode.pdx, landed): pure in-process
#      light-vs-heavy classifier + indirector that reads a command's
#      resource_mask u32 from offset 84 of its CommandSig record
#      (R222.M2 reserved-tail carve-out) and routes dispatch to one
#      of two weak-import function-pointer slots. `_dm_init` is a
#      pure-leaf idempotent boot hook that zero-fills five u64 scalar
#      .bss slots (`_dm_light_fn`, `_dm_spawn_fn`, `_dm_light_count`,
#      `_dm_heavy_count`, `_dm_last_decision`); .bss zero-init at
#      program load already satisfies the boot semantic and the init
#      exists for test-time resets. `_dm_register_light` and
#      `_dm_register_spawn` are pure-leaf publishers for the two
#      weak-import slots; both reject `fn_ptr == 0` with
#      DM_ERR_NULL_FN. `_dm_classify` is a pure leaf that validates
#      the CommandSig record (cs_body != 0, cs_len >= 128, magic ==
#      'CSIG' at offset 0) then ANDs the resource_mask u32 at offset
#      84 against DM_HEAVY_MASK (0x3C = NET|EXEC|LONG_RUNNING|
#      HIGH_MEM) via the imm8 variant of `and r64, imm8` -- never
#      `and r64, imm64`. `_dm_dispatch` has one 4-push callee-save
#      frame with +8 pad, CALLs `_dm_classify` for the decision,
#      bumps the matching counter and sets `_dm_last_decision`, then
#      indirect-calls through `[_dm_light_fn]` or `[_dm_spawn_fn]`
#      (precedent: script_cmd.pdx:660 `mov rax, [slot_ptr]; call
#      rax`). No KIND; no external module dependency; no cross-
#      library dependency. The two weak-import slots mirror the
#      R133.M5 `_tcg_check_fn` / R133.M6 `_sc_dispatch_fn` precedent
#      byte-for-byte minus the klog_s1 emit (user-space has no klog
#      surface; the fingerprint instead lives in the two u64
#      counters a smoke-mode asserter reads). Error band 0x4800..
#      0x48FF (7 slots used; 0x4807..0x48FF reserved for M6.1+).
#   R224.M1 LambdaLit parser: pure in-process byte-walker + header /
#      descriptor emitter over the caller's NFC-normalised input and
#      caller-supplied out buffer. _ll_parse CALLs the module-private
#      _ll_skip_ws / _ll_classify_type / _ll_parse_param helpers. No
#      KIND; no external module dependency.
#   R224.M2 ClosureCapture parser (closure_capture.pdx): pure
#      in-process byte-walker + header + Binding emitter over the
#      caller's NFC-normalised input and caller-supplied out buffer.
#      _cc_parse CALLs the module-private _cc_skip_ws / _cc_parse_binding
#      helpers; _cc_parse_binding in turn CALLs _cc_skip_ws and
#      _cc_classify_type leaves. No KIND; no external module dependency.
#      Parses the OPTIONAL closure-capture list `[binding, binding, ...]`
#      that signals the lambda will cross a process boundary (Q13
#      hybrid serialization). Untyped bindings capture BY_REF (name
#      resolves at receiver); typed bindings `name:type` capture
#      BY_VALUE (sender serializes the value using the declared type).
#   R224.M3 EffectRow (effect_row.pdx): pure in-process effect-row
#      parser + Rémy-style subtype check layered over R225.M2
#      RowTypes. `_er_init` lazy-populates the 32-slot label-intern
#      table (6 primitives + 26 user-declared slots) from a 96-byte
#      static source table. `_er_label_lookup` and `_er_label_intern`
#      are self-contained scanners over this module's own .bss.
#      `_er_skip_ws` is a pure-leaf WS walker. `_er_parse` consumes
#      `WS* ! WS* { LabelList? } ` and builds a RowTypes row by
#      calling `_rt_row_empty` / `_rt_row_var` / `_rt_row_extend`
#      (intra-library cross-module calls into row_types.pdx).
#      `_er_check_subtype` walks the sub row and calls `_rt_find` +
#      `_rt_row_select` on each ROW_EXT label, returning
#      ER_ERR_IMPURE_PASSED_PURE with the offending packed label id
#      when sub carries a label absent from sup. `_er_render` round-
#      trips the row back to source form, calling `_rt_find` on each
#      step. No KIND; no external cross-library dependency (intra-
#      library dep on RowTypes/HmCore for the row-graph pool and
#      allocators -- see linker-dependencies section below).
#      Treats effect labels and effect-row types as pure type-level
#      artefacts; no capability handle flows through this module.
#   R224.M4 CapRow (cap_row.pdx, landed): pure in-process capability-
#      row parser + env-mask covering check layered over R225.M2
#      RowTypes. `_cr_init` lazy-populates the 32-slot label-intern
#      table (10 primitives + 22 user-declared slots) from a 160-byte
#      static source table. `_cr_label_lookup` and `_cr_label_intern`
#      are self-contained scanners over this module's own .bss.
#      `_cr_skip_ws` is a pure-leaf WS walker. `_cr_parse` consumes
#      `WS* @ WS* { LabelList? } ` and builds a RowTypes row by
#      calling `_rt_row_empty` / `_rt_row_var` / `_rt_row_extend`
#      (intra-library cross-module calls into row_types.pdx).
#      `_cr_check_env` walks the required row and calls `_rt_find`
#      on each cursor, then bit-tests the caller-supplied `env_mask`
#      at the packed-id-extracted idx; returns
#      `CR_ERR_MISSING_CAP` with the offending packed label id when
#      env lacks a required cap (the `E0820_MISSING_CAP` diagnostic).
#      `_cr_render` round-trips the row back to source form, calling
#      `_rt_find` on each step. No KIND; no external cross-library
#      dependency (intra-library dep on RowTypes/HmCore for the row-
#      graph pool and allocators -- see linker-dependencies section
#      below). Capability labels and capability rows are pure type-
#      level artefacts; no capability handle flows through this
#      module (the kernel-side cap table bridges in at a later M4.8).
#   R224.M5 LetScope (let_scope.pdx, landed): pure in-process lexical
#      scope frame pool backing nested lambdas + `let` / `let rec`
#      bindings per standard HM shadowing. Working-memory substrate:
#      a 128-slot ring of 32-byte scope frames (slot 0 reserved as
#      the null-sentinel so `parent_frame_ref == 0` means "no
#      enclosing scope"). `_ls_init` is a pure-leaf idempotent boot
#      hook that reserves slot 0 by setting `_ls_frame_next := 1` on
#      a cold .bss (the .bss zero-init at program load already
#      satisfies the "zero-fill pool" semantic). `_ls_push_let`,
#      `_ls_push_letrec`, `_ls_push_lambda` are thin wrappers over a
#      shared `_ls_push_impl` helper (sub rsp,8 + mov r8,kind + CALL
#      + add rsp,8 + RET; r8 selects 1 SCOPE_LET / 2 SCOPE_LETREC /
#      3 SCOPE_LAMBDA). `_ls_push_impl` validates name_len in
#      [1..16] and kind in [1..3], pool-not-full, writes the 32-byte
#      header (kind u16, flags u16, parent u32, name_inline u8[16],
#      name_len u8, 3 reserved u8, type_scheme_ref u32), bumps
#      `_ls_frame_next`, returns the pre-increment slot index.
#      `_ls_resolve` walks the parent chain starting at the input
#      frame_ref inner-first comparing name_len then bytes; on
#      first byte-match returns `(type_scheme_ref << 32) | LS_OK`;
#      on chain-end (cursor==0) returns `LS_ERR_NOT_FOUND`; on
#      cursor >= 128 or kind==0 mid-walk returns `LS_ERR_BAD_FRAME`;
#      on bad input name_len returns `LS_ERR_BAD_NAME`. Shadowing
#      is natural (inner match wins). `_ls_pop` is a pure-leaf
#      read-only accessor returning the parent u32 at
#      `&_ls_frame_pool + frame_ref*32 + 4`; the pool is append-
#      only within a parse pass (the enclosing cursor is restored
#      by the AST driver). The `type_scheme_ref` u32 payload is
#      caller-opaque: at raw M5 the HM elaborator passes a HmCore
#      pool_idx; at the M5.1 wire-up a TypeEnv scheme_id is used
#      instead (flags bit 0 discriminates). No KIND; no external
#      cross-library dependency; NO intra-library dependency at M5
#      (R225.M1 HmCore and R229.M3 TypeEnv interpretations of the
#      stored u32 live at the R229.M4+ REPL-dispatch layer, not in
#      THIS module). Treats scope frames as pure parse-time working-
#      memory artefacts; no capability handle flows through this
#      module.
#   R224.M6+ lambda-lang follow-ups: linear/affine propagation (M7)
#      consumes the Q-A2 lattice-aware CapRow enforcement planned
#      at M4.7. First-class pipeline value (M6) consumes R220.M7
#      closure arena. Still no KIND surface in this library -- the
#      enclosing shell session is where effect / cap row ids reify
#      against the KIND-touching tier.
#   R225.M1 HM algorithm W core: pure in-process type-graph walker
#      over a singleton .bss pool (2048-byte TypeNode storage) and
#      the caller-supplied scheme buffers. _hm_fresh_var /
#      _hm_unify / _hm_instantiate / _hm_generalise all touch only
#      the module's own .bss + caller-pointer args. _hm_unify and
#      _hm_occurs are self-recursive via the symbol table; _hm_find
#      is a pure leaf. No KIND; no external module dependency.
#   R225.M2 Row types (row_types.pdx): pure in-process row-graph
#      walker + Remy-style unifier layered over R225.M1's singleton
#      _hm_pool. _rt_find walks the extended resolved chain (TyVar
#      OR ROW_VAR). _rt_alloc_node reserves a 16-byte slot shared
#      with hm_core allocations. _rt_label_hash is a pure-leaf
#      FNV-1a 32 over caller bytes. _rt_row_empty / _rt_row_var /
#      _rt_row_extend are single-nested-CALL allocators. _rt_record_type
#      allocates TyApp(TyCon(RECORD,1), row). _rt_row_select /
#      _rt_row_restrict / _rt_row_concat walk the row chain and
#      allocate new ROW_EXT nodes for restrict/concat results.
#      _rt_row_unify is self-recursive and cross-recursive with
#      _hm_unify (TyVar and TyCon arms delegate; TyApp recurses on
#      children because they may be rows; TyRow uses the Remy pivot
#      on label mismatch). No KIND; no external cross-library
#      dependency (intra-library dep on HmCore for _hm_unify and
#      the _hm_pool / _hm_pool_next / _hm_var_next .bss symbols).
#   R225.M3+ typechecker follow-ups: Datalog predicate types (M3)
#      bridge SchemasSig descriptors (R222.M1) into the pool via a
#      1:1 remap table; cross-context flow (M5) chains R225.M2 row
#      shapes through pipeline <-> Datalog boundaries; rank-
#      restricted enforcement (M6) adds a scheme-depth counter.
#      None introduces a KIND surface this library invokes against.
#   R225.M4 EffectUnify (effect_unify.pdx, landed): pure in-process
#      effect-row join (least-upper-bound over the monotone effect
#      lattice) + rank-restricted-quantifier (P10) well-formedness
#      validator. Layered over R225.M2 RowTypes (the Rémy row
#      primitives + the shared singleton _hm_pool). `_eu_unify(row_a,
#      row_b)` walks both inputs collecting packed label ids (opaque
#      u32 identity; same encoding R224.M3 EffectRow and R224.M4
#      CapRow use), notes any ROW_VAR tail, and rebuilds a single
#      row containing the set union of labels with the appropriate
#      tail (fresh ROW_VAR if either input is open; ROW_EMPTY
#      otherwise). The dedup check during the prepend loop reuses
#      `_rt_row_select` (R225.M2) so the dedup discipline matches
#      the one `_rt_row_restrict` / `_rt_row_concat` already enforce.
#      `_eu_check_rank(scheme_ptr, scheme_len)` validates a HmCore
#      scheme byte stream against P10: at M4 the wire format carries
#      a SINGLE outer ∀ so the check is a well-formedness validator
#      (header consistency; n_bound_vars <= 64; n_body_nodes in
#      [1..128]; every body node's kind in {TYVAR, TYCON, TYAPP,
#      TYROW}). `EU_ERR_RANK_RESTRICTED_VIOLATION` is reserved for
#      the M4.1 wire-format extension that lands nested-quantifier
#      body nodes. `_eu_least(rows_ptr, n)` folds `_eu_unify` across
#      N rows (join is associative + commutative, so fold order is
#      irrelevant); caps n at EU_MAX_JOIN_ARITY=16. All three entry
#      points return packed_u64 `(joined_row_ref << 32) | status`
#      with status in band 0x4900..0x4907. No KIND; no external
#      cross-library dependency (intra-library dep on RowTypes +
#      HmCore for the row-graph pool and allocators -- see linker-
#      dependencies section below). Treats effect labels and effect
#      rows as pure type-level artefacts; no capability handle flows
#      through this module.
#   R226.M1 Datalog parser: pure in-process byte-walker + Clause-
#      record emitter over the caller's NFC-normalised input and
#      caller-supplied out buffer. _dl_parse CALLs the module-
#      private _dl_skip_ws / _dl_scan_ident_or_var / _dl_scan_number
#      / _dl_scan_string / _dl_scan_body helpers. No KIND; no
#      external module dependency.
#   R226.M2+ datalog follow-ups: predicate-type resolution (M2)
#      calls into R220.M4 schema registry via linker-resolved
#      symbol; evaluator (M3+) runs over R127.M7 history_facts via
#      the direct-call API _hf_query_by_* (which the shell owns, not
#      this library). This library stays leaf.
#   R229.M2 SessionEnv (session_env.pdx): pure in-process persistent
#      binding store over a singleton .bss pool (8 KiB env pool + 64 B
#      head-table). _se_init / _se_init_session are pure leaves that
#      touch only this module's own .bss. _se_insert_binding /
#      _se_lookup_binding / _se_unset_binding are pure-leaf scanners
#      over the per-session row with 6-push callee-save frames and no
#      nested CALLs. The type-pool interpretation of the stored
#      type_ref u32 is HmCore's responsibility (SessionEnv does NOT
#      call into HmCore -- the shell-side REPL dispatch, at R229.M3+,
#      does, and merely hands the pool_idx through). No KIND; no
#      external module dependency; no cross-library dependency.
#   R229.M3 TypeEnv (type_env.pdx): pure in-process type-scheme store
#      + specialisation cache over singleton .bss pools (32 KiB scheme
#      pool, 8 KiB cache pool, 64 B head-table). `_te_init_session` is
#      a pure leaf that touches only this module's own .bss.
#      `_te_insert_scheme` / `_te_evict_scheme` are pure-leaf scanners
#      with 6-push callee-save frames and no nested CALLs.
#      `_te_specialize` CALLs `_hm_instantiate` (R225.M1, hm_core.pdx)
#      on every cache miss -- the ONE cross-module nested CALL in this
#      module. The scheme byte stream is a verbatim HmCore scheme wire
#      format; TypeEnv stores and forwards the bytes without
#      interpretation. No KIND; no cross-library dependency; intra-
#      library dependency on HmCore via `_hm_instantiate`.
#   R229.M4+ REPL evaluator follow-ups: dispatch (M3+ in the kernel-
#      side layer) parses `let`/`unset` from the R229.M1 line_buf,
#      calls HM typecheck + evaluator and routes into THIS module +
#      SessionEnv. Teardown cascade wire-up (M4) folds
#      `_se_init_session` AND `_te_init_session` into
#      `_shell_session_destroy`. Exported bindings (M4) use the
#      SessionEnv flags byte + a TypeEnv-side cross-session export
#      flag. Lexical nested scopes (M5) add a stack of SessionEnv
#      rows per session; TypeEnv's scheme ids remain session-flat.
#      Persistent per-user env (M6) layers a pdxfs serialisation hook
#      over both SessionEnv and TypeEnv. None introduces a KIND
#      surface this library invokes against.
#
# None of the planned landings is expected to introduce a KIND
# surface this library itself invokes against. The parser is a
# passive linker artifact.
#
# declares_output_schemas: none. The parser emits no semantic-pipe
# records; its only user-visible outputs are the packed-u64 return
# values documented at each entry point in src/*.pdx. A downstream
# consumer (e.g. the shell's lexer at R221.M4+, the LSP bridge at
# R221.M6) that chooses to log a parse fingerprint does so via its
# own `klog_s1_*` wrapper on its own schema -- this library's
# primitives neither call klog nor know about one.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2700..0x27FF (R221.M1, utf8_nfc) -------------------
#
# Small-value user-space packed-status range. Four slots used at M1:
#
#   U8N_OK                 : 0        normalise succeeded.
#   U8N_ERR_INVALID_UTF8   : 0x2700   input not RFC 3629 well-formed.
#   U8N_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x2701   out_cap < NFC output byte count.
#   U8N_ERR_NORMALIZE_FAIL : 0x2702   reserved for post-M1 normaliser-
#                                     internal failure (never returned
#                                     at M1).
#
# The 0x2700..0x27FF range is reserved for parser-tier packed-status
# codes across R221. The remaining 0x2703..0x27FF slots are reserved
# for M2+ error kinds (e.g. GRAPHEME_INVALID_UTF8 at M2, LEX_UNEXPECTED
# _TOKEN at M4, AST_ARENA_FULL at M5).
#
# ---- Error band 0x2B00..0x2BFF (R223.M1, pipeline) -------------------
#
# Pipeline-tier packed-status range. Five slots used at R223.M1:
#
#   PL_OK                     : 0        parse succeeded.
#   PL_ERR_TOO_MANY_STAGES    : 0x2B00   > PL_MAX_STAGES (16).
#   PL_ERR_TOO_MANY_ARGS      : 0x2B01   > PL_MAX_ARGS (8) per stage.
#   PL_ERR_UNTERMINATED_QUOTE : 0x2B02   DQ or SQ open at EOI.
#   PL_ERR_EMPTY_STAGE        : 0x2B03   `||`, leading or trailing `|`.
#   PL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL      : 0x2B04   out_cap < needed stage count * 64.
#
# The 0x2B00..0x2BFF range is reserved for pipeline-lang parser
# packed-status codes across R223. Slots 0x2B05..0x2BFF reserved for
# R223.M2+ (redir ops, @hostname annotations, etc.).
#
# Not to be confused with the kernel-side Pipeline module's
# PL_ERR_BAD_ARGS / PL_ERR_TOO_MANY / PL_ERR_DST_OVERFLOW codes which
# occupy a wholly separate 0xFFFFEC40..42 band and name a different
# (planner-side) module.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2C00..0x2CFF (R224.M1, lambda_lit) ----------------
#
# Lambda-lang parser-tier packed-status range. Five slots used at
# R224.M1:
#
#   LL_OK                  : 0        parse succeeded.
#   LL_ERR_SYNTAX          : 0x2C00   grammar mismatch at ident,
#                                     ':', '(', ')', or ','.
#   LL_ERR_TOO_MANY_PARAMS : 0x2C01   > LL_MAX_PARAMS (8).
#   LL_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE    : 0x2C02   type_name not in the M1 set
#                                     ({u64,i64,str,hex,hash32,tsc,
#                                       path,pid}).
#   LL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL   : 0x2C03   out_cap < 32 + n_params*32 +
#                                     body_len.
#   LL_ERR_NO_ARROW        : 0x2C04   ParamList terminator was not
#                                     `->` (dedicated code so the
#                                     diagnostic can point at the
#                                     missing-arrow site rather than
#                                     at a generic SYNTAX).
#
# The 0x2C00..0x2CFF range is reserved for lambda-lang parser packed-
# status codes across R224. Slots 0x2C05..0x2CFF reserved for R224.M2+
# (expression parse, effect-row inference, capability-row typing,
# nested-lambda scoping, destructuring-pattern mismatch, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3600..0x36FF (R225.M2, row_types) ------------------
#
# Typechecker-tier packed-status range for the SECOND R225 wave --
# ROW TYPES: Remy-style row polymorphism for records with named
# fields, layered over R225.M1's TypeNode pool. Seven slots used at
# R225.M2:
#
#   RT_OK                 : 0        row op succeeded.
#   RT_ERR_LABEL_MISSING  : 0x3600   _rt_row_select/_rt_row_restrict
#                                    label not found in row.
#   RT_ERR_LABEL_DUP      : 0x3601   _rt_row_concat label collision.
#   RT_ERR_POOL_FULL      : 0x3602   HmCore pool exhausted (shared
#                                    with hm_core; row allocations
#                                    draw from the same singleton
#                                    _hm_pool).
#   RT_ERR_KIND_MISMATCH  : 0x3603   _rt_row_unify saw a row-vs-non-row
#                                    pair where kinds disagree.
#   RT_ERR_CLOSED_ROW     : 0x3604   _rt_row_unify saw EMPTY vs EXT;
#                                    _rt_row_concat refused an open
#                                    (ROW_VAR-tailed) first operand.
#   RT_ERR_OCCURS         : 0x3605   reserved for M4+ row-var cycle
#                                    detection (M2 relies on hm_core's
#                                    TyVar occurs-check for shared
#                                    type-level cycles; the row-var
#                                    chain depth is bounded by pool
#                                    size, so a dedicated row-occurs
#                                    check is a conservative no-op at
#                                    M2 and the slot is reserved).
#   RT_ERR_MISMATCH       : 0x3606   field-type unification failure
#                                    bubbled up from a nested
#                                    _rt_row_unify or _hm_unify call;
#                                    equivalent at the top-level
#                                    protocol surface to hm_core's
#                                    HM_ERR_MISMATCH (0x2D01) but
#                                    carried in the row-tier band so
#                                    the caller's error path can
#                                    discriminate "row operation
#                                    failed" from "pure HM operation
#                                    failed".
#
# The 0x3600..0x36FF range is reserved for R225.M2+ row types. Slots
# 0x3607..0x36FF reserved for R225.M3 (predicate-type bridge),
# R225.M5 (cross-context flow), R225.M6 (rank-2 refusal), and R225.M7
# (error-span wrapping). R225.M4 (effect-row unification) landed in
# its OWN disjoint band 0x4900..0x49FF (effect_unify.pdx) rather than
# subdividing this band -- the two row-tier submodules (RowTypes
# structural unify vs EffectUnify join) require distinguishable
# compound-error dispatch, so disjoint bands keep the discrimination
# straightforward.
#
# R225.M1 (hm_core) owns the disjoint 0x2D00..0x2DFF band; the two
# R225 submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "pure HM
# operation failed" from "row operation failed". The parallel
# R224.M2 band (0x3500..0x35FF) and R229.M2 band (0x3700..0x37FF)
# sit outside this range; the three parallel M2 arms of Wave 117
# chose non-adjacent slices to simplify the disjointness proof.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2D00..0x2DFF (R225.M1, hm_core) --------------------
#
# Typechecker-tier packed-status range. Four slots used at R225.M1:
#
#   HM_OK                 : 0        unification / instantiation /
#                                    generalisation succeeded.
#   HM_ERR_OCCURS         : 0x2D00   cyclic unification caught by the
#                                    occurs-check (TyVar binds to a
#                                    type that mentions itself).
#   HM_ERR_MISMATCH       : 0x2D01   constructor or arity mismatch;
#                                    also returned on malformed scheme
#                                    (bad body-relative index, unknown
#                                    kind code, env ref out-of-range).
#   HM_ERR_POOL_FULL      : 0x2D02   128-node TypeNode pool exhausted.
#   HM_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x2D03   out_cap < scheme-size required by
#                                    _hm_generalise, or scheme_len
#                                    inconsistent with its header at
#                                    _hm_instantiate.
#
# The 0x2D00..0x2DFF range is reserved for R225 typechecker packed-
# status codes. Slots 0x2D04..0x2DFF reserved for R225.M2+ (row-type
# mismatches, effect-row saturation, rank-2 refusal, missing predicate
# schema, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3500..0x35FF (R224.M2, closure_capture) ------------
#
# Lambda closure-capture parser-tier packed-status range. Six slots
# used at R224.M2:
#
#   CC_OK                    : 0        parse succeeded.
#   CC_ERR_SYNTAX            : 0x3500   grammar mismatch at ident, ':',
#                                       ',', or peek after ident.
#   CC_ERR_TOO_MANY_BINDINGS : 0x3501   > CC_MAX_BINDINGS (16).
#   CC_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE      : 0x3502   type_name not in the M2 set
#                                       ({u64,i64,str,hex,hash32,tsc,
#                                         path,pid}).
#   CC_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL     : 0x3503   out_cap < 32 + n_bindings*32.
#   CC_ERR_NO_OPEN           : 0x3504   first non-whitespace byte was
#                                       not `[`.
#   CC_ERR_NO_CLOSE          : 0x3505   EOI before matching `]`.
#
# The 0x3500..0x35FF range is reserved for the R224.M2 closure-capture
# parser band. R224.M1 (LambdaLit) owns a disjoint 0x2C00..0x2CFF band
# -- the two R224 submodules do not share status codes because a
# downstream dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the
# lambda header faulted" from "the explicit capture list faulted".
# Slots 0x3506..0x35FF reserved for R224.M3+ (per-binding effect-row
# mismatch, capability-row mismatch, let-rec recursive capture failure,
# linear/affine propagation violation, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3700..0x37FF (R229.M2, session_env) ----------------
#
# Session-env packed-status range for the R229 REPL-evaluator wave.
# Five slots used at R229.M2:
#
#   SE_OK                   : 0        operation succeeded.
#   SE_ERR_BAD_SESSION      : 0x3700   session_id >= SE_MAX_SESSIONS (8).
#   SE_ERR_BAD_NAME         : 0x3701   name_len == 0 or > SE_NAME_MAX (16).
#   SE_ERR_TOO_MANY         : 0x3702   head == SE_MAX_BINDINGS (32) on
#                                      insert of a new (not-yet-present)
#                                      name.
#   SE_ERR_NOT_FOUND        : 0x3703   lookup or unset against a name
#                                      not present in the session env
#                                      (or present only as a tombstone).
#   SE_ERR_BAD_SCHEME_KIND  : 0x3704   insert called with scheme_kind
#                                      not in {SE_SCHEME_DIRECT (1),
#                                      SE_SCHEME_BLOB (2)}.
#
# The 0x3700..0x37FF range is reserved for the R229 session-env band.
# R229.M1 (kernel-side REPL loop) owns a disjoint 0x3000..0x30FF band
# (RL_ERR_*) -- the two R229 submodules do not share status codes
# because a downstream dispatcher's compound error path must
# distinguish "the per-cycle state machine faulted" from "the
# session-scoped binding store faulted". Slots 0x3705..0x37FF reserved
# for R229.M3+ (SE_ERR_HM_POOL_FULL when SessionEnv proxies the HM
# layer's pool-full, SE_ERR_TOMBSTONE_EXHAUSTED on compaction failure,
# SE_ERR_EXPORTED_IMMUTABLE on cross-session rebind of an exported
# binding, etc.).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3D00..0x3DFF (R229.M3, type_env) -------------------
#
# Type-env packed-status range for the R229 REPL-evaluator wave's M3
# landing (type-scheme store + specialisation cache). Nine slots used:
#
#   TE_OK                   : 0        operation succeeded.
#   TE_ERR_BAD_SESSION      : 0x3D00   session_id >= TE_MAX_SESSIONS (8).
#   TE_ERR_BAD_SCHEME_ID    : 0x3D01   scheme_id not in [1..TE_MAX_SCHEMES
#                                      (16)].
#   TE_ERR_NOT_FOUND        : 0x3D02   scheme_id slot is empty / evicted,
#                                      or scheme_id > scheme_count.
#   TE_ERR_TOO_MANY         : 0x3D03   insert on a session whose
#                                      scheme_count has reached
#                                      TE_MAX_SCHEMES (16).
#   TE_ERR_BAD_LEN          : 0x3D04   scheme_len < TE_SCHEME_HDR_MIN (8)
#                                      or > TE_SCHEME_PAYLOAD_MAX (248).
#   TE_ERR_HM_POOL_FULL     : 0x3D05   `_hm_instantiate` returned
#                                      HM_ERR_POOL_FULL (0x2D02).
#   TE_ERR_HM_MISMATCH      : 0x3D06   `_hm_instantiate` returned
#                                      HM_ERR_MISMATCH (0x2D01).
#   TE_ERR_HM_OUT_TOO_SMALL : 0x3D07   `_hm_instantiate` returned
#                                      HM_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL (0x2D03).
#   TE_ERR_HM_OCCURS        : 0x3D08   `_hm_instantiate` returned
#                                      HM_ERR_OCCURS (0x2D00) -- won't
#                                      happen on a well-formed scheme;
#                                      reserved for future call sites
#                                      that unify through here.
#
# The 0x3D00..0x3DFF range is reserved for the R229.M3 type-env band.
# R229.M1 owns 0x3000..0x30FF (kernel-side RL_*); R229.M2 owns
# 0x3700..0x37FF (SessionEnv SE_*). The three R229 submodules do not
# share status codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound error
# path must distinguish "the per-cycle state machine faulted" from
# "the session-scoped binding store faulted" from "the scheme store /
# instantiate cache faulted". Slots 0x3D09..0x3DFF reserved for
# R229.M4+ (TE_ERR_CROSS_SESSION on an export-flag violation,
# TE_ERR_SCHEME_VERSION_MISMATCH on a persisted-env load, etc.).
#
# The 0x3C00..0x3CFF slice between the R222.M3 (0x3900..0x39FF) /
# R133 kernel-side (0x3A00..0x3BFF) bands and this one is now the
# landed R222.M4 ArgSpec+FlagSpec carve-out (see the dedicated
# section below).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3800..0x38FF (R221.M2, grapheme_iter) --------------
#
# TR#29 grapheme-cluster-boundary iterator packed-status range.
#
#   GI_STATUS_OK           : 0        advance/retreat succeeded.
#   GI_STATUS_EOF          : 1        _gi_next_cluster: cursor_byte at EOI.
#   GI_STATUS_BOF          : 1        _gi_prev_cluster: cursor_byte at 0.
#   GI_ERR_INVALID_UTF8    : 0x3800   substrate (libpdx-unicode-tables
#                                     R131.M2 _gc_next) returned the
#                                     INVALID_UTF8 status; propagated
#                                     through with cursor_byte preserved.
#   GI_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL   : 0x3801   _gi_tokenize_args: out_cap < the
#                                     emitted descriptor stride.
#   GI_ERR_TOO_MANY_TOKENS : 0x3802   _gi_tokenize_args: emitted token
#                                     count > GI_MAX_TOKENS.
#   GI_ERR_BAD_CURSOR      : 0x3803   _gi_prev_cluster: cursor_byte >
#                                     bytes_len.
#
# The 0x3800..0x38FF range is reserved for grapheme-iterator packed-
# status codes across R221.M2+. R221.M1 (UTF-8 + NFC decoder) owns a
# disjoint parser-tier band -- the two R221 submodules do not share
# status codes because a downstream dispatcher must distinguish
# "the decoder faulted" from "the cluster iterator faulted". Slots
# 0x3804..0x38FF reserved for R221.M3+ follow-ups (width-pass
# TR#11 integration, line-break TR#14 integration).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3900..0x39FF (R222.M3, functor_instance) ----------
#
# Functor-instantiation materialization-record packed-status range.
#
#   FI_OK                 : 0        parse + elaboration succeeded.
#   FI_ERR_SYNTAX         : 0x3900   bad grammar at current cursor.
#   FI_ERR_NAME_MISMATCH  : 0x3901   parsed name does not match a
#                                    functor in the CommandSig body
#                                    (R222.M2) catalogue.
#   FI_ERR_TOO_MANY_ARGS  : 0x3902   arg_count > FI_MAX_ARGS (16).
#   FI_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x3903   out_cap < 64 + arg_count*32.
#   FI_ERR_BAD_CS_RECORD  : 0x3904   command-sig record magic mismatch
#                                    (cs_len < 128 or cs magic != CSIG;
#                                    also materialization record magic
#                                    mismatch not FINS).
#   FI_ERR_ELABORATION    : 0x3905   per-arg elaboration failed.
#   FI_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE   : 0x3906   per-arg type_code not in the
#                                    expected set for the functor's
#                                    typed signature.
#
# The 0x3900..0x39FF range is reserved for functor-instantiation
# packed-status codes across R222.M3+. R222.M1/M2 (SchemasSig,
# CommandSig) own disjoint 0x3200/0x3300 bands -- the three R222
# submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "schemas-sig
# faulted" vs "command-sig faulted" vs "functor-instantiation
# faulted". Slots 0x3907..0x39FF reserved for R222.M4+ follow-ups
# (ArgSpec typing failures, FlagSpec typing failures, registry
# miss, commands.toml bind failure, describe-rendering failure,
# per-turn fuzz-corpus deviations).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3C00..0x3CFF (R222.M4, arg_flag_spec) --------------
#
# ArgSpec + FlagSpec typing packed-status range.
#
#   AFS_OK                     : 0        parse / check succeeded.
#   AFS_ERR_SYNTAX             : 0x3C00   grammar fault in a spec body.
#   AFS_ERR_UNKNOWN_TYPE       : 0x3C01   type_name not in the M4 set
#                                         ({u64,i64,str,hex,hash32,tsc,
#                                           path,pid}).
#   AFS_ERR_TOO_MANY_ARGS      : 0x3C02   > AFS_MAX_ARGS (16).
#   AFS_ERR_TOO_MANY_FLAGS     : 0x3C03   > AFS_MAX_FLAGS (16).
#   AFS_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL      : 0x3C04   out_cap < n_records * 32.
#   AFS_ERR_BAD_INVOCATION     : 0x3C05   _afs_check_invocation:
#                                         invocation missing 'FINS'
#                                         magic or inv_len < 64 +
#                                         arg_count * 32.
#   AFS_ERR_TYPE_MISMATCH      : 0x3C06   invocation byte run does
#                                         not parse as the ArgSpec /
#                                         FlagSpec's declared type.
#   AFS_ERR_MISSING_REQUIRED   : 0x3C07   non-OPTIONAL ArgSpec not
#                                         consumed by the invocation.
#   AFS_ERR_UNKNOWN_FLAG       : 0x3C08   invocation flag not in the
#                                         FlagSpec table.
#   AFS_ERR_FLAG_NO_VALUE      : 0x3C09   TAKES_VALUE flag at EOI.
#   AFS_ERR_EXTRA_POS          : 0x3C0A   positional past last ArgSpec
#                                         with no VARIADIC slot.
#
# The 0x3C00..0x3CFF range is reserved for ArgFlagSpec packed-status
# codes across R222.M4+. R222.M1/M2/M3 (SchemasSig, CommandSig,
# FunctorInstance) own disjoint 0x2A00/0x3300/0x3900 bands -- the
# four R222 submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "schemas-sig
# faulted" vs "command-sig faulted" vs "functor-instantiation
# faulted" vs "arg/flag-spec faulted". Slots 0x3C0B..0x3CFF reserved
# for R222.M5 (registry-client reconcile errors) and R222.M6
# (commands.toml bind errors). The 0x3B00..0x3BFF band is reserved
# for the parallel R133.M4 kernel-side arm of this wave; 0x3A00..
# 0x3AFF is live (R133.M3 pds import graph, Wave 118). ArgFlagSpec's
# 0x3C00..0x3CFF carve-out sits on a non-adjacent kilo-step boundary
# so the four R222 submodule bands can all be disambiguated by a
# simple compound-error dispatcher.
#
# ---- Error band 0x3400..0x34FF (R223.M2, record_projection) ----------
#
# Pipeline-tier packed-status range for the SECOND R223 wave --
# RECORD PROJECTION, the `select FIELDS` / `project FIELDS` pipeline
# operators that filter the typed-record stream by field name. Three
# slots used at R223.M2:
#
#   RP_OK                  : 0        parse succeeded.
#   RP_ERR_SYNTAX          : 0x3400   grammar mismatch (bad first byte,
#                                     empty field, > 14-byte name,
#                                     missing or trailing comma, EOI
#                                     before any field).
#   RP_ERR_TOO_MANY_FIELDS : 0x3401   > RP_MAX_FIELDS (32).
#   RP_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL   : 0x3402   out_cap < n_fields * 16.
#
# The 0x3400..0x34FF range is reserved for record-projection packed-
# status codes across R223.M2+. R223.M1 (pipeline stage parser) owns
# a disjoint 0x2B00..0x2BFF band -- the two R223 modules do not share
# status codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound error path
# must distinguish "the outer pipeline tokeniser faulted" from "the
# inner RecordProjection argv parser faulted". Slots 0x3403..0x34FF
# reserved for R223.M3+ (differentiation between `select` reorder
# semantics and `project` drop-unselected semantics; wildcards; name
# aliases).
#
# The 0x2F00..0x32FF gap between the R226 band (0x2EFF) and the new
# R222.M2 CommandSig band (0x3300..0x33FF, documented below) is
# reserved for R227+ parser-tier primitives (pds container header
# parse, pipeline-record row types, Datalog predicate-type bridge,
# etc.) that will land before R223.M3's semantic split.
#
# ---- Error band 0x3300..0x33FF (R222.M2, command_sig) ----------------
#
# Cmd-functor-identity parser packed-status range. Four slots used at
# R222.M2:
#
#   CS_OK                     : 0        parse succeeded.
#   CS_ERR_SYNTAX             : 0x3300   grammar mismatch at keyword,
#                                        ':', '"', hex rights, or ident
#                                        byte-class.
#   CS_ERR_TOO_MANY_CAPS      : 0x3301   > CS_MAX_CAPS (8).
#   CS_ERR_UNKNOWN_STABILITY  : 0x3302   stability value not in the
#                                        {stable, experimental,
#                                         deprecated} set.
#   CS_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL      : 0x3303   out_cap < CS_HEADER_BYTES (128)
#                                        + n_caps * CS_CAP_DESC_BYTES
#                                        (32).
#
# The 0x3300..0x33FF range is reserved for the R222 cmd-functor-identity
# parser band. R222.M1 (SchemasSig) owns a disjoint 0x2A00..0x2AFF
# band -- the two R222 submodules do not share status codes because a
# downstream dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the
# input/output record shape faulted" from "the functor identity
# declaration faulted". Slots 0x3304..0x33FF reserved for R222.M3+
# (REPL dispatch typecheck mismatch, ArgSpec/FlagSpec parse errors,
# registry client lookup miss, etc.).
#
# Not to be confused with the kernel-side Pipeline module's
# PL_ERR_BAD_ARGS / PL_ERR_TOO_MANY / PL_ERR_DST_OVERFLOW codes which
# occupy a wholly separate 0xFFFFEC40..42 band and name a different
# (planner-side) module.
#
# ---- Error band 0x2E00..0x2EFF (R226.M1, datalog) --------------------
#
# Datalog-tier packed-status range. Five slots used at R226.M1:
#
#   DL_OK                      : 0        parse succeeded.
#   DL_ERR_SYNTAX              : 0x2E00   grammar mismatch.
#   DL_ERR_TOO_MANY_CLAUSES    : 0x2E01   > DL_MAX_CLAUSES (256).
#   DL_ERR_TOO_MANY_TERMS      : 0x2E02   > DL_MAX_TERMS (4) per head.
#   DL_ERR_UNTERMINATED_STRING : 0x2E03   `"..."` open at EOI.
#   DL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL       : 0x2E04   out_cap < needed clause count * 48.
#
# The 0x2E00..0x2EFF range is reserved for datalog parser packed-
# status codes across R226 (slots 0x2E05..0x2EFF reserved for M2+
# predicate-type resolution, semi-naive evaluator, aggregation,
# stratified negation, session-local EDB, etc.).
#
# The 0x2C00..0x2CFF range (previously documented as "R225.M*
# reserved" in pipeline.pdx's namespace map) is now the live R224
# lambda-lang band. R225.M1 consumes the 0x2D00..0x2DFF slice of the
# former shared reservation; R226 carves out 0x2E00..0x2EFF cleanly
# above that. R223.M2 (RecordProjection) carves 0x3400..0x34FF
# ABOVE the contiguous R221..R226 block rather than reusing the
# adjacent 0x2B05..0x2BFF slot of R223.M1's pipeline band -- the
# two R223 submodules remain error-disjoint so a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path can distinguish outer-pipeline
# faults from inner-projection faults. The pipeline.pdx comment-
# level reservation note is superseded by this caps.decl entry.
#
# R224.M2 (ClosureCapture) carves 0x3500..0x35FF; R225.M2 (RowTypes)
# carves 0x3600..0x36FF; R229.M2 (SessionEnv) carves 0x3700..0x37FF.
# The three M2 bands of Wave 117 sit on non-adjacent kilo-step
# boundaries so a downstream dispatcher's compound error path can
# discriminate at a glance which satellite submodule faulted, and
# the slices are large enough to accommodate the full M-wave
# decomposition each submodule declares.
#
# R221.M2 (GraphemeIter) carves 0x3800..0x38FF; R222.M3 (FunctorInstance)
# carves 0x3900..0x39FF. Both land in Wave 118 on non-adjacent kilo-step
# boundaries disjoint from every prior wave's bands.
#
# R222.M4 (ArgFlagSpec) carves 0x3C00..0x3CFF in Wave 119. The adjacent
# 0x3A00..0x3AFF is R133.M3 kernel-side (pds import graph, landed in
# Wave 118); 0x3B00..0x3BFF is reserved for the parallel R133.M4
# kernel arm of this wave. All three land on non-adjacent kilo-step
# boundaries disjoint from every prior wave's bands.
#
# R229.M3 (TypeEnv) carves 0x3D00..0x3DFF. The 0x3A00..0x3BFF kernel-
# side bands (R133.M3+M4 import graph + resolution cache) and the
# 0x3C00..0x3CFF R222.M4 ArgSpec reservation sit between the Wave-118
# bands and the TypeEnv band, giving TypeEnv a disjoint kilo-step
# carve-out with headroom for M4+ follow-ups.
#
# R221.M3 (WidthPass) carves 0x3F00..0x3FFF. The 0x3E00..0x3EFF band
# sits between the TypeEnv band and this one and is reserved for the
# parallel R133.M5 kernel-side arm. WidthPass's carve-out sits on a
# non-adjacent kilo-step boundary disjoint from every prior wave's
# bands and leaves 254 reserved slots (0x3F02..0x3FFF) for M3.1+
# follow-ups (locale-amb precise table, Hangul-Jamo scalar handling,
# TR#14 line-break integration).
#
# R221.M4 (CtxLexer) carves 0x4200..0x42FF in Wave 121. The
# 0x4000..0x40FF slot is R224.M3 EffectRow (landed in Wave 120);
# 0x4100..0x41FF is reserved for the parallel R133.M6 kernel-side
# arm of this wave. CtxLexer's carve-out sits on a new kilo-step
# boundary disjoint from every prior wave's bands, with 247
# reserved slots (0x4208..0x42FF) for M4.1+ follow-ups (bad-UTF-8
# byte in a code-point run, M5 keyword-set growth, long-identifier
# cap, etc.).
#
# R224.M4 (CapRow) carves 0x4300..0x43FF in Wave 121 (parallel to
# R221.M4 CtxLexer above). The 0x4000..0x40FF slot is R224.M3
# EffectRow (sibling in the R224 wave); 0x4100..0x41FF reserved for
# the parallel R133.M6 kernel arm; 0x4200..0x42FF R221.M4 CtxLexer
# (parallel in Wave 121). CapRow's carve-out sits on a new kilo-step
# boundary disjoint from every prior wave's bands, with 246 reserved
# slots (0x430A..0x43FF) for M4.1+ follow-ups (duplicate-label
# SYNTAX refinement, open-row discipline tighten, per-row-var naming,
# `_cr_declare` BAD_NAME, LambdaLit splice-point diagnostics, Q-A2
# substructural-lattice violations).
#
# ---- Error band 0x3F00..0x3FFF (R221.M3, width_pass) -----------------
#
# TR#11 East-Asian-Width parser-tier packed-status range.
#
#   WP_OK                     : 0        operation succeeded.
#   WP_ERR_INVALID_UTF8       : 0x3F00   _wp_cols: _gi_next_cluster
#                                        reported invalid UTF-8 at the
#                                        current cursor; partial
#                                        accumulator still meaningful.
#   WP_ERR_BAD_LOCALE_WIDTH   : 0x3F01   _wp_set_locale_amb: width
#                                        argument not in {1, 2}.
#
# The 0x3F00..0x3FFF range is reserved for width-pass parser-tier
# packed-status codes across R221.M3+. R221.M1 (utf8_nfc) owns a
# disjoint 0x2700..0x27FF slice; R221.M2 (grapheme_iter) owns
# 0x3800..0x38FF -- the three R221 submodules do not share status
# codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound error path must
# distinguish "the decoder faulted" from "the cluster iterator
# faulted" from "the width pass faulted". Slots 0x3F02..0x3FFF
# reserved for R221.M3.1+ follow-ups (locale-amb precise overlay
# faults, Hangul-Jamo scalar handling faults, TR#14 line-break
# integration faults).
#
# R224.M3 (EffectRow) carves 0x4000..0x40FF in Wave 120. The
# 0x3E00..0x3EFF slot is reserved for the parallel R133.M5 kernel
# arm; 0x3F00..0x3FFF is R221.M3 (parallel WidthPass arm, above).
# EffectRow's carve-out sits on a new kilo-step boundary disjoint
# from every prior wave's bands, with 248 reserved slots
# (0x4008..0x40FF) for M3.1+ follow-ups (duplicate-label SYNTAX
# refinement, open-row subtype tightening, per-row-var naming,
# `_er_declare` user-declared-effect intern surface, LambdaLit
# integration diagnostics).
#
# ---- Error band 0x4000..0x40FF (R224.M3, effect_row) ----------------
#
# Lambda-lang effect-polymorphism parser-tier packed-status range.
# Eight slots used at R224.M3:
#
#   ER_OK                      : 0        operation succeeded.
#   ER_ERR_SYNTAX              : 0x4000   grammar fault at `!`, `{`,
#                                         `,`, `}`, or an identifier
#                                         byte run; also returned by
#                                         `_er_parse` on count >= 16
#                                         (annotation too wide at M3).
#   ER_ERR_UNKNOWN_LABEL       : 0x4001   `_er_parse` saw a non-primitive
#                                         identifier that is not yet
#                                         interned (M3 does not yet
#                                         expose `_er_declare`;
#                                         `_er_parse` treats intern-miss
#                                         on a non-primitive as unknown).
#   ER_ERR_LABEL_TABLE_FULL    : 0x4002   `_er_label_intern` on a full
#                                         32-slot table (6 primitives +
#                                         26 user-declared cap).
#   ER_ERR_IMPURE_PASSED_PURE  : 0x4003   `_er_check_subtype` saw a
#                                         label present in sub but
#                                         absent in sup; the offending
#                                         packed label id (tag<<24 |
#                                         idx) is in the high 32 bits
#                                         of the packed-u64 return.
#   ER_ERR_POOL_FULL           : 0x4004   HmCore pool exhausted during
#                                         `_rt_row_extend` or
#                                         `_rt_row_var` inside the
#                                         `_er_parse` build phase.
#   ER_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL       : 0x4005   `_er_render`: out_cap smaller
#                                         than the rendered byte count.
#   ER_ERR_KIND_MISMATCH       : 0x4006   `_er_check_subtype` or
#                                         `_er_render` saw a non-row
#                                         kind on the walked cursor
#                                         (schema violation; propagated
#                                         from the row-walk guard).
#   ER_ERR_UNKNOWN_ROWVAR      : 0x4007   reserved for M3.3 when
#                                         `_er_render` learns per-row-
#                                         var naming (currently emits
#                                         bare "rho" for every
#                                         ROW_VAR tail).
#
# The 0x4000..0x40FF range is reserved for effect-row parser-tier
# packed-status codes across R224.M3+. R224.M1 (lambda_lit) owns
# the disjoint 0x2C00..0x2CFF slice; R224.M2 (closure_capture) owns
# 0x3500..0x35FF -- the three R224 submodules do not share status
# codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound error path must
# distinguish "the lambda header faulted" from "the capture list
# faulted" from "the effect annotation faulted". Slots 0x4008..
# 0x40FF reserved for R224.M3.1+ (duplicate-label SYNTAX code,
# open-row subtype tighten diagnostics, per-row-var naming errors,
# `_er_declare` BAD_NAME, LambdaLit splice-point diagnostics,
# capability-row parallel at R224.M4).
#
# Not to be confused with R225.M2 RowTypes (`_rt_row_*`) which
# owns the row-graph band 0x3600..0x36FF; EffectRow REUSES
# RowTypes allocators (`_rt_row_empty`, `_rt_row_var`,
# `_rt_row_extend`, `_rt_find`, `_rt_row_select`) via the
# intra-library linker-dep list below and interprets a RowTypes
# row's arg0 slot as a packed `(tag, idx)` label id rather than
# an FNV-1a 32 hash; the row-aware unifier handles both
# interpretations verbatim because label identity reduces to
# `cmp label_a, label_b` on the 32-bit arg0 slot in both
# flavours.
#
# ---- Error band 0x4200..0x42FF (R221.M4, ctx_lexer) -----------------
#
# Context-tracking lexer parser-tier packed-status range. Eight slots
# used at R221.M4:
#
#   CL_OK                      : 0        operation succeeded.
#   CL_ERR_SYNTAX              : 0x4200   unrecognised byte at the
#                                         current cursor (control
#                                         char, UTF-8 high byte,
#                                         misplaced punctuator including
#                                         bare `-` or `?`); also returned
#                                         by `_cl_lex_token` on failed
#                                         two-byte-operator lookahead
#                                         (`-` without `>`, `?` without
#                                         `-`).
#   CL_ERR_STACK_OVERFLOW      : 0x4201   `_cl_push_ctx` or the internal
#                                         `{`-push path on depth == 16.
#   CL_ERR_STACK_UNDERFLOW     : 0x4202   `_cl_pop_ctx` on depth == 0.
#   CL_ERR_UNMATCHED_BRACE     : 0x4203   `_cl_lex_token` saw `}` with
#                                         depth == 0 at emit time (not
#                                         yet reduced to STACK_UNDERFLOW
#                                         because the `}` byte has not
#                                         yet consumed; the diagnostic
#                                         points at the brace).
#   CL_ERR_PIPE_IN_DATALOG     : 0x4204   `|` in CTX_DATALOG (datalog
#                                         grammar reserves `|` for
#                                         future disjunction syntax at
#                                         R226.M2+ and refuses it at
#                                         M4; the two-byte neighbour
#                                         `||` is not yet recognised).
#   CL_ERR_UNTERMINATED_STRING : 0x4205   `"` with no closing `"` before
#                                         EOI. Returned on EOI inside
#                                         `cl_lt_string_scan` or inside
#                                         an unterminated `\<EOI>` escape.
#   CL_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL       : 0x4206   `_cl_tokenize`: out_cap smaller
#                                         than the next 16-byte Token
#                                         record stride.
#   CL_ERR_BAD_CTX             : 0x4207   `_cl_push_ctx` on ctx > 2.
#
# The 0x4200..0x42FF range is reserved for context-tracking-lexer
# parser-tier packed-status codes across R221.M4+. R221.M1 (utf8_nfc)
# owns the disjoint 0x2700..0x27FF slice; R221.M2 (grapheme_iter)
# owns 0x3800..0x38FF; R221.M3 (width_pass) owns 0x3F00..0x3FFF --
# the four R221 submodules do not share status codes because a
# downstream dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish
# "the decoder faulted" from "the cluster iterator faulted" from
# "the width pass faulted" from "the context-tracking lexer faulted".
# Slots 0x4208..0x42FF reserved for R221.M4.1+ follow-ups
# (bad-UTF-8 byte in a code-point run, M5 keyword-set growth,
# long-identifier cap, etc.).
#
# Not to be confused with R221.M1..M3 bands above or with the
# user-side kernel-parallel 0x4100..0x41FF slot reserved for the
# R133.M6 kernel arm of this wave.
#
# ---- Error band 0x4300..0x43FF (R224.M4, cap_row) --------------------
#
# Lambda-lang capability-row-typing parser-tier packed-status range.
# Ten slots used at R224.M4:
#
#   CR_OK                      : 0        operation succeeded.
#   CR_ERR_SYNTAX              : 0x4300   grammar fault at `@`, `{`,
#                                         `,`, `}`, or an identifier
#                                         byte run; also returned by
#                                         `_cr_parse` on count >= 16
#                                         (annotation too wide at M4).
#   CR_ERR_UNKNOWN_CAP         : 0x4301   `_cr_parse` saw a non-primitive
#                                         identifier that is not yet
#                                         interned (M4 does not yet
#                                         expose `_cr_declare`;
#                                         `_cr_parse` treats intern-miss
#                                         on a non-primitive as unknown).
#                                         Maps to the `E0822_UNKNOWN_CAP`
#                                         diagnostic.
#   CR_ERR_LABEL_TABLE_FULL    : 0x4302   `_cr_label_intern` on a full
#                                         32-slot table (10 primitives +
#                                         22 user-declared cap).
#   CR_ERR_MISSING_CAP         : 0x4303   `_cr_check_env` saw a label
#                                         present in required_row but
#                                         absent in env_mask; the
#                                         offending packed label id
#                                         (tag<<24 | idx) is in the
#                                         high 32 bits of the packed-u64
#                                         return. Maps to the
#                                         `E0820_MISSING_CAP` diagnostic
#                                         family -- the acceptance
#                                         anchor for the issue brief's
#                                         8-lambda adversarial test
#                                         (one lambda per primitive cap
#                                         0..7, env_mask=0, each
#                                         returning (packed_id_i << 32)
#                                         | 0x4303).
#   CR_ERR_POOL_FULL           : 0x4304   HmCore pool exhausted during
#                                         `_rt_row_extend` or
#                                         `_rt_row_var` inside the
#                                         `_cr_parse` build phase.
#   CR_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL       : 0x4305   `_cr_render`: out_cap smaller
#                                         than the rendered byte count.
#   CR_ERR_KIND_MISMATCH       : 0x4306   `_cr_check_env` or
#                                         `_cr_render` saw a non-row
#                                         kind on the walked cursor
#                                         (schema violation; propagated
#                                         from the row-walk guard).
#   CR_ERR_UNSATISFIABLE_ROW   : 0x4307   reserved for M4.2 open-row
#                                         discipline tighten (open row-
#                                         var tail against closed env
#                                         must bind to empty before OK).
#                                         Maps to `E0821_UNSATISFIABLE_ROW`.
#   CR_ERR_INFLATED_ROW        : 0x4308   reserved for M4.7 Q-A2
#                                         substructural-lattice enforce
#                                         (linear caps row-ext cannot
#                                         repeat at a call site). Maps
#                                         to `E0823_INFLATED_ROW`.
#   CR_ERR_UNKNOWN_ROWVAR      : 0x4309   reserved for M4.3 when
#                                         `_cr_render` learns per-row-
#                                         var naming (currently emits
#                                         bare "rho" for every
#                                         ROW_VAR tail).
#
# The 0x4300..0x43FF range is reserved for capability-row parser-tier
# packed-status codes across R224.M4+. R224.M1 (lambda_lit) owns the
# disjoint 0x2C00..0x2CFF slice; R224.M2 (closure_capture) owns
# 0x3500..0x35FF; R224.M3 (effect_row) owns 0x4000..0x40FF -- the
# four R224 submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the lambda
# header faulted" from "the capture list faulted" from "the effect
# annotation faulted" from "the capability annotation faulted".
# Slots 0x430A..0x43FF reserved for R224.M4.1+ (duplicate-label
# SYNTAX code, open-row discipline tighten diagnostics, per-row-var
# naming errors, `_cr_declare` BAD_NAME, LambdaLit splice-point
# diagnostics, Q-A2 linear-cap repeat violations).
#
# Diagnostic-family mapping (E0820 family per the issue brief):
#   E0820_MISSING_CAP       -> CR_ERR_MISSING_CAP        (0x4303)
#   E0821_UNSATISFIABLE_ROW -> CR_ERR_UNSATISFIABLE_ROW  (0x4307)
#   E0822_UNKNOWN_CAP       -> CR_ERR_UNKNOWN_CAP        (0x4301)
#   E0823_INFLATED_ROW     -> CR_ERR_INFLATED_ROW       (0x4308)
#
# CapRow REUSES RowTypes allocators (`_rt_row_empty`, `_rt_row_var`,
# `_rt_row_extend`, `_rt_find`) via the intra-library linker-dep
# list below -- same convention as R224.M3 EffectRow. The two row-
# flavour parsers interpret the RowTypes arg0 slot via per-table
# packed `(tag, idx)` ids; `_rt_row_unify` handles both flavours
# verbatim because label identity reduces to a 32-bit `cmp` on
# arg0 and the per-table packed ids are statically disjoint across
# tables.
#
# ---- Error band 0x4500..0x45FF (R222.M5, cmd_registry) ---------------
#
# Command-registry client packed-status range. Six slots used at
# R222.M5:
#
#   CMDREG_OK                   : 0        operation succeeded.
#   CMDREG_ERR_NOT_FOUND        : 0x4501   `_cmdreg_lookup` found no
#                                          entry with matching
#                                          name_hash on the probe
#                                          chain.
#   CMDREG_ERR_BAD_SCOPE        : 0x4502   `_cmdreg_register` with
#                                          scope not in {0, 1}
#                                          (CMDREG_SCOPE_SYSTEM /
#                                          CMDREG_SCOPE_USER).
#   CMDREG_ERR_BAD_NAME         : 0x4503   `_cmdreg_register` or
#                                          `_cmdreg_lookup` with
#                                          name_len == 0 or
#                                          name_len > CMDREG_NAME_MAX
#                                          (= 16).
#   CMDREG_ERR_TABLE_FULL       : 0x4504   `_cmdreg_register` with all
#                                          128 slots occupied (probe
#                                          wrapped to the starting
#                                          slot).
#   CMDREG_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL    : 0x4505   `_cmdreg_dump` out_cap <
#                                          n_occupied *
#                                          CMDREG_ENTRY_BYTES (= 48).
#
# The 0x4500..0x45FF range is reserved for command-registry client
# packed-status codes across R222.M5+. R222.M1 (schemas_sig) owns the
# disjoint 0x2A00..0x2AFF slice; R222.M2 (command_sig) owns
# 0x3300..0x33FF; R222.M3 (functor_instance) owns 0x3900..0x39FF;
# R222.M4 (arg_flag_spec) owns 0x3C00..0x3CFF -- the five R222
# submodules do not share status codes because a downstream dispatcher's
# compound error path must distinguish "schemas-sig faulted" vs
# "command-sig faulted" vs "functor-instantiation faulted" vs
# "arg/flag-spec faulted" vs "registry client faulted". Slots
# 0x4506..0x45FF reserved for R222.M6 (commands.toml bind failures),
# R222.M7 (fuzz corpus deviations), R222.M8 (describe-render failures).
#
# The 0x4400..0x44FF slot is the parallel R221.M5 Ast arm of this wave
# (Wave 122, landed below). CmdRegistry's 0x4500..0x45FF carve-out
# sits on a non-adjacent kilo-step boundary disjoint from every prior
# landed wave's bands.
#
# ---- Error band 0x4400..0x44FF (R221.M5, ast) ------------------------
#
# Unified AST allocator + renderer packed-status range. Six slots used
# at R221.M5:
#
#   AST_OK                 : 0        operation succeeded.
#   AST_ERR_POOL_FULL      : 0x4400   `_ast_alloc`: `_ast_pool_next >=
#                                     AST_POOL_CAP` (256). Returned as
#                                     a bare rax value because `_ast_
#                                     alloc` returns a node_ref u64;
#                                     0 == pool-full sentinel.
#   AST_ERR_BAD_REF        : 0x4401   `_ast_render`: `node_ref == 0`
#                                     OR `node_ref >= _ast_pool_next`.
#                                     The three setters silent-no-op
#                                     on the same condition rather
#                                     than returning a status (their
#                                     signatures are void).
#   AST_ERR_BAD_KIND       : 0x4402   reserved for M5.1+ kind-table
#                                     enforcement (M5 trusts caller;
#                                     the AST module does not validate
#                                     the SyntaxKind u16 against the
#                                     family enum, deferring that
#                                     check to a stricter M5.1 pass).
#   AST_ERR_OUT_TOO_SMALL  : 0x4403   `_ast_render`: `out_cap <
#                                     src_length` (the span would
#                                     overflow the caller's out buffer).
#   AST_ERR_SPAN_OOB       : 0x4404   `_ast_render`: `src_offset +
#                                     src_length > _ast_src_len` (the
#                                     node's recorded span exceeds the
#                                     caller's set source buffer).
#   AST_ERR_NO_SOURCE      : 0x4405   `_ast_render`: `_ast_src_ptr ==
#                                     0`; the caller forgot to call
#                                     `_ast_set_source` after
#                                     `_ast_init`.
#
# The 0x4400..0x44FF range is reserved for the R221.M5 ast band.
# R221.M1 (utf8_nfc) owns the disjoint 0x2700..0x27FF slice;
# R221.M2 (grapheme_iter) owns 0x3800..0x38FF; R221.M3 (width_pass)
# owns 0x3F00..0x3FFF; R221.M4 (ctx_lexer) owns 0x4200..0x42FF -- the
# five R221 submodules do not share status codes because a downstream
# dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the decoder
# faulted" from "the cluster iterator faulted" from "the width pass
# faulted" from "the context-tracking lexer faulted" from "the AST
# allocator / renderer faulted". Slots 0x4406..0x44FF reserved for
# R221.M5.1+ (kind-table enforcement, cycle-detect on child_ref walks,
# synthetic-span discipline, child-aware render diagnostics).
#
# Not to be confused with the parallel R222.M5 CmdRegistry band at
# 0x4500..0x45FF (also Wave 122): the two Wave-122 submodules sit on
# adjacent kilo-step boundaries but are otherwise disjoint; the
# compound-error dispatcher reads `(status & 0xFF00) == 0x4400` for
# AST faults vs `== 0x4500` for registry faults.
#
# ---- Error band 0x4600..0x46FF (R224.M5, let_scope) ------------------
#
# Lambda-lang nested-lambda + `let` / `let rec` scope-frame-pool
# packed-status range. Five slots used at R224.M5:
#
#   LS_OK                      : 0        operation succeeded.
#   LS_ERR_POOL_FULL           : 0x4600   push on a full _ls_frame_pool
#                                         (128 slots total, slot 0 is
#                                         the null-sentinel so 127
#                                         usable); the 128th push
#                                         returns 0 and bumps nothing.
#                                         The `E0833_POOL_FULL`
#                                         diagnostic.
#   LS_ERR_NOT_FOUND           : 0x4601   `_ls_resolve` reached the
#                                         chain-end (cursor == 0)
#                                         without a byte-level name
#                                         match on any frame; the
#                                         `E0830_NAME_NOT_FOUND`
#                                         diagnostic.
#   LS_ERR_BAD_FRAME           : 0x4602   `_ls_resolve` encountered a
#                                         cursor >= 128 or a kind==0
#                                         slot-sentinel mid-walk; the
#                                         `E0831_BAD_FRAME` diagnostic.
#   LS_ERR_BAD_NAME            : 0x4603   push or resolve with
#                                         `name_len == 0` or
#                                         `name_len > LS_NAME_MAX`
#                                         (= 16); the
#                                         `E0832_BAD_NAME` diagnostic.
#   LS_ERR_BAD_KIND            : 0x4604   `_ls_push_impl` with kind
#                                         not in {SCOPE_LET=1,
#                                         SCOPE_LETREC=2,
#                                         SCOPE_LAMBDA=3}; internal
#                                         consistency check -- the
#                                         three named push wrappers
#                                         hard-code the kind so this
#                                         is reachable only if a
#                                         future caller invokes
#                                         `_ls_push_impl` directly
#                                         with a bad r8. The
#                                         `E0834_BAD_KIND` diagnostic.
#
# The 0x4600..0x46FF range is reserved for let-scope parser-tier
# packed-status codes across R224.M5+. R224.M1 (lambda_lit) owns the
# disjoint 0x2C00..0x2CFF slice; R224.M2 (closure_capture) owns
# 0x3500..0x35FF; R224.M3 (effect_row) owns 0x4000..0x40FF; R224.M4
# (cap_row) owns 0x4300..0x43FF -- the five R224 submodules do not
# share status codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound
# error path must distinguish "the lambda header faulted" from "the
# capture list faulted" from "the effect annotation faulted" from
# "the capability annotation faulted" from "the scope frame pool
# faulted". Slots 0x4605..0x46FF reserved for R224.M5.1+ follow-ups
# (TypeEnv scheme_id reinterpretation, letrec-group batch push,
# LambdaLit splice-point diagnostics, compacting pop semantics,
# proptest-harness-driven invariants).
#
# Diagnostic-family mapping (E0830 family per the issue brief):
#   E0830_NAME_NOT_FOUND    -> LS_ERR_NOT_FOUND     (0x4601)
#   E0831_BAD_FRAME         -> LS_ERR_BAD_FRAME     (0x4602)
#   E0832_BAD_NAME          -> LS_ERR_BAD_NAME      (0x4603)
#   E0833_POOL_FULL         -> LS_ERR_POOL_FULL     (0x4600)
#   E0834_BAD_KIND          -> LS_ERR_BAD_KIND      (0x4604)
#
# R224.M5 LetScope carves 0x4600..0x46FF in Wave 122 (co-landed with
# the parallel R221.M5 Ast arm at 0x4400..0x44FF and the R222.M5
# CmdRegistry arm at 0x4500..0x45FF). The three Wave-122 arms sit on
# three contiguous kilo-step boundaries that are disjoint from every
# prior landed wave's bands; LetScope's slice is non-adjacent to the
# parallel-arm slices (gap at 0x4500..0x45FF is CmdRegistry; LetScope
# leap-frogs past the two parallel arms to 0x4600) so a compound-
# error dispatcher reads `(status & 0xFF00) == 0x4400` for AST faults,
# `== 0x4500` for registry faults, and `== 0x4600` for scope-frame
# faults.
#
# Not to be confused with R225.M1 HmCore (`_hm_pool`) which LetScope
# does NOT call into at M5 -- the `type_scheme_ref` u32 is stored
# verbatim and the HM-dispatch interpretation lives at the R229.M4+
# REPL layer; no intra-library linker dep.
#
# ---- Error band 0x4700..0x47FF (R221.M6, span_map) -------------------
#
# Source-span tracking across UTF-8 -> NFC normalization packed-status
# range. Four slots used at R221.M6:
#
#   SM_OK                      : 0        operation succeeded.
#   SM_ERR_POOL_FULL           : 0x4700   `_sm_record_pair`:
#                                         `_sm_pair_count >=
#                                         SM_POOL_CAP` (1024). The
#                                         pair pool is `.bss` 8 KiB
#                                         (1024 slots x 8 B stride);
#                                         exhaustion signals an
#                                         adversarial input with
#                                         > 1024 NFC composition
#                                         boundaries in a single parse.
#   SM_ERR_NON_MONOTONIC       : 0x4701   `_sm_record_pair`: new
#                                         `nfc_offset` <= previous
#                                         pair's `nfc_offset` OR new
#                                         `src_offset` <= previous
#                                         pair's `src_offset`. Pairs
#                                         must be strictly monotonic
#                                         on both coordinates;
#                                         defensive catch for walker
#                                         bugs in `_sm_from_u8nfc`.
#   SM_ERR_OOB_OFFSET          : 0x4702   reserved for R221.M6.1+
#                                         when the pair fields widen
#                                         to u64 or an input-length
#                                         overflow guard is added.
#   SM_ERR_BAD_INPUT           : 0x4703   `_sm_from_u8nfc`: null
#                                         pointer in `src_ptr` or
#                                         `nfc_ptr`. Pre-prologue
#                                         bail with no frame to tear
#                                         down.
#
# The 0x4700..0x47FF range is reserved for span-map parser-tier
# packed-status codes across R221.M6+. R221.M1 (utf8_nfc) owns the
# disjoint 0x2700..0x27FF slice; R221.M2 (grapheme_iter) owns
# 0x3800..0x38FF; R221.M3 (width_pass) owns 0x3F00..0x3FFF; R221.M4
# (ctx_lexer) owns 0x4200..0x42FF; R221.M5 (ast) owns 0x4400..0x44FF
# -- the six R221 submodules do not share status codes because a
# downstream dispatcher's compound error path must distinguish "the
# decoder faulted" from "the cluster iterator faulted" from "the
# width pass faulted" from "the context-tracking lexer faulted" from
# "the AST allocator / renderer faulted" from "the span map faulted".
# Slots 0x4704..0x47FF reserved for R221.M6.1+ follow-ups (per-pair
# invalid UTF-8 code, bounded-window resync exhaustion, cross-
# NFC-form interop, u64-width pair fields).
#
# SpanMap carves 0x4700..0x47FF in Wave 123 (co-landed with the
# parallel R222.M6 DispatchMode arm at 0x4800..0x48FF and the
# R225.M4 EffectUnify arm at 0x4900..0x49FF). The three Wave-123
# arms sit on three contiguous kilo-step boundaries that are
# disjoint from every prior landed wave's bands; SpanMap's slice is
# adjacent-below DispatchMode so a compound-error dispatcher reads
# `(status & 0xFF00) == 0x4700` for span-map faults, `== 0x4800`
# for dispatch-mode faults, and `== 0x4900` for effect-row-join /
# rank-check faults.
#
# Pack shape for `_sm_lookup`:
#
#   rax = src_offset u64        -- the mapped source byte offset
#                                  (identity map when no pair applies).
#
# Pack shape for `_sm_record_pair` and `_sm_from_u8nfc`:
#
#   rax = errno u64             -- SM_OK (0) or SM_ERR_* (0x4700..).
#
# Not to be confused with R221.M1 Utf8Nfc (`_u8n_decode_and_normalize`)
# which owns the normalization proper; this module layers a sideband
# table underneath M1's output and does NOT call into M1 itself at
# raw M6 (the caller passes both buffers in by pointer).
#
# ---- Error band 0x4800..0x48FF (R222.M6, dispatch_mode) --------------
#
# Light-vs-heavy dispatch-mode packed-status range. Seven slots used
# at R222.M6:
#
#   DM_OK                   : 0        operation / dispatch succeeded
#                                      (DM_LIGHT also == 0; the two
#                                      names overload the same value
#                                      because a LIGHT classification
#                                      is itself the OK status for
#                                      `_dm_classify`).
#   DM_HEAVY                : 1        classifier returned HEAVY.
#   DM_ERR_BAD_RECORD       : 0x4800   `_dm_classify` with cs_body==0,
#                                      cs_len<128, or magic mismatch
#                                      (not 'CSIG' at offset 0).
#   DM_ERR_NO_LIGHT_FN      : 0x4801   `_dm_dispatch` LIGHT path with
#                                      `_dm_light_fn == 0`.
#   DM_ERR_NO_SPAWN_FN      : 0x4802   `_dm_dispatch` HEAVY path with
#                                      `_dm_spawn_fn == 0`.
#   DM_ERR_NULL_FN          : 0x4803   `_dm_register_light` or
#                                      `_dm_register_spawn` called
#                                      with `fn_ptr == 0`.
#   DM_ERR_LIGHT_FAILED     : 0x4804   `_dm_light_fn` returned non-
#                                      zero errno; errno is packed
#                                      into bits [63:32] of the
#                                      dispatch return.
#   DM_ERR_SPAWN_FAILED     : 0x4805   `_dm_spawn_fn` returned non-
#                                      zero errno; errno is packed
#                                      into bits [63:32].
#   DM_ERR_BAD_MAT          : 0x4806   `_dm_dispatch` with mat_body==0
#                                      or mat_len < DM_FI_HEADER_BYTES_MIN
#                                      (= 64).
#
# The 0x4800..0x48FF range is reserved for dispatch-mode packed-
# status codes across R222.M6+. R222.M1 (schemas_sig) owns the
# disjoint 0x2A00..0x2AFF slice; R222.M2 (command_sig) owns
# 0x3300..0x33FF; R222.M3 (functor_instance) owns 0x3900..0x39FF;
# R222.M4 (arg_flag_spec) owns 0x3C00..0x3CFF; R222.M5 (cmd_registry)
# owns 0x4500..0x45FF -- the six R222 submodules do not share
# status codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound error
# path must distinguish each submodule's faults. Slots 0x4807..
# 0x48FF reserved for R222.M6.1+ follow-ups (per-cost budget
# violation, cross-session dispatch policy, cap-mask narrowing
# mismatch, registration overwrite guard, per-session counter
# table).
#
# The 0x4700..0x47FF slot is the parallel R221.M6 SpanMap arm of this
# wave (Wave 123, landed above); 0x4900..0x49FF is the parallel
# R225.M4 EffectUnify arm (Wave 123, landed below). DispatchMode's
# 0x4800..0x48FF carve-out sits on a kilo-step boundary disjoint
# from every prior landed wave's bands and sits between the two
# sibling Wave-123 arms so a compound-error dispatcher reads
# `(status & 0xFF00) == 0x4700` for span-map faults, `== 0x4800`
# for dispatch-mode faults, and `== 0x4900` for effect-row-join /
# rank-check faults.
#
# Pack shape for `_dm_dispatch`:
#
#   bits [15: 0]  status   DM_OK or DM_ERR_*
#   bit  [16]     decision 0 = LIGHT, 1 = HEAVY
#   bits [63:32]  errno    downstream errno on *_FAILED paths; 0 else
#
# Resource-mask bits (DispatchMode interpretation, resource_mask u32
# at [cs_body + 84]):
#
#   DM_BIT_FS_READ       : 0x01   reads filesystem bytes
#   DM_BIT_FS_WRITE      : 0x02   writes filesystem bytes
#   DM_BIT_NET           : 0x04   makes outbound network connections
#   DM_BIT_EXEC          : 0x08   invokes other processes
#   DM_BIT_LONG_RUNNING  : 0x10   may run past the per-turn deadline
#   DM_BIT_HIGH_MEM      : 0x20   retains a large working set
#   DM_HEAVY_MASK        : 0x3C   NET | EXEC | LONG_RUNNING | HIGH_MEM
#
# Classification: LIGHT iff (resource_mask & DM_HEAVY_MASK) == 0;
# HEAVY otherwise. The AND encodes as `and r64, imm8` (0x3C has bit
# 7 clear) and is explicitly permitted by feedback_pdx_encoder_pitfalls
# ("name-length mask / bit tests use imm8 variants only"; precedent
# grapheme_iter.pdx:335 `and r11, 0xFF`).
#
# ---- Error band 0x4900..0x49FF (R225.M4, effect_unify) ---------------
#
# Typechecker-tier effect-row join + rank-restricted-quantifier packed-
# status range. Eight slots used at R225.M4:
#
#   EU_OK                            : 0        operation succeeded.
#   EU_ERR_KIND_MISMATCH             : 0x4900   `_eu_unify` saw a non-
#                                               TyRow kind on a walked
#                                               cursor (schema violation;
#                                               propagated from the row-
#                                               walk guard, matching the
#                                               R224.M3 ER_ERR_KIND_
#                                               MISMATCH + R224.M4
#                                               CR_ERR_KIND_MISMATCH
#                                               convention).
#   EU_ERR_POOL_FULL                 : 0x4901   HmCore pool exhausted
#                                               during `_rt_row_var` or
#                                               `_rt_row_extend` inside
#                                               the `_eu_unify` build
#                                               phase.
#   EU_ERR_RANK_RESTRICTED_VIOLATION : 0x4902   reserved for R225.M4.1
#                                               HmCore wire-format
#                                               extension (nested-
#                                               quantifier body nodes;
#                                               `_eu_check_rank`'s raw-
#                                               M4 pass validates only
#                                               shape + legal kinds and
#                                               returns BAD_SCHEME on
#                                               every reachable
#                                               violation).
#   EU_ERR_BAD_SCHEME                : 0x4903   `_eu_check_rank` saw a
#                                               malformed scheme byte
#                                               stream: header truncated;
#                                               scheme_len inconsistent
#                                               with header; n_bound_vars
#                                               > 64; n_body_nodes
#                                               outside [1..128]; or a
#                                               body node with kind byte
#                                               outside {TYVAR=1, TYCON=
#                                               2, TYAPP=3, TYROW=4}.
#   EU_ERR_EMPTY_ARRAY               : 0x4904   `_eu_least` with n == 0;
#                                               the join over an empty
#                                               set is undefined at the
#                                               protocol surface.
#   EU_ERR_TOO_MANY                  : 0x4905   `_eu_unify` with per-
#                                               row raw-collect count
#                                               > EU_MAX_LABELS_PER_ROW
#                                               (16) or combined count
#                                               > EU_MAX_RAW_LABELS
#                                               (32); `_eu_least` with
#                                               n > EU_MAX_JOIN_ARITY
#                                               (16).
#   EU_ERR_ROWVAR_OCCURS             : 0x4906   reserved for R225.M4.2
#                                               inner-subterm Rémy
#                                               unify arm; cycle during
#                                               pivot-binding of two
#                                               open-tail inputs.
#   EU_ERR_UNIFY_INCONSISTENT        : 0x4907   reserved for R225.M4.2
#                                               inner-subterm Rémy
#                                               unify arm; per-pivot
#                                               type-level conflict
#                                               bubbled up from an
#                                               inner `_rt_row_unify`.
#
# The 0x4900..0x49FF range is reserved for effect-row-join + rank-
# restricted-quantifier packed-status codes across R225.M4+. R225.M1
# (hm_core) owns the disjoint 0x2D00..0x2DFF slice; R225.M2 (row_
# types) owns 0x3600..0x36FF -- the three R225 submodules do not
# share status codes because a downstream dispatcher's compound
# error path must distinguish "pure HM operation faulted" from
# "row operation faulted" from "effect-row join / rank check
# faulted". Slots 0x4908..0x49FF reserved for R225.M4.1+ follow-ups
# (effect-flow error chains, label-alphabet domain errors, per-
# session effect-decl collision diagnostics, row-fingerprint cache
# miss diagnostics).
#
# EffectUnify REUSES RowTypes allocators (`_rt_row_empty`, `_rt_row_
# var`, `_rt_row_extend`, `_rt_find`, `_rt_row_select`) via the
# intra-library linker-dep list below -- same convention as R224.M3
# EffectRow and R224.M4 CapRow. The arg0 u32 slot is treated as an
# OPAQUE packed label id so the identity comparison reduces to a
# 32-bit `cmp` on arg0 which works equally for R224.M3 effect-
# labels AND R224.M4 capability-labels (ready for the R225.M4.3
# capability-row-join parallel landing).
#
# Pack shape (common across all three entries):
#   bits [31: 0]   status     EU_OK or EU_ERR_*
#   bits [63:32]   row_ref    pool_idx of the joined row on OK; 0 on
#                             error.
#
# ---- Disjointness proof (all bands) ----------------------------------
#
# All codes fit in a 32-bit unsigned, placed in the low 32 bits of
# packed returns. Disjoint from every other user-space packed-status
# range in the paideia-os tree:
#
#   * libpdx-unicode-tables UTF-8 band: 0xFFFFE700..0xFFFFE70F (large;
#                                       returned raw, not packed)
#   * libpdx-unicode-tables M2..M7 bands: 0xFFFFE710..0xFFFFE77F (large)
#   * libpdx-elevate: 0xFFFFE5E0..EF, 0xFFFFEA00..7F (large)
#   * libpdx-volume internal 0x0100-band (lpv_errors.pdx)
#   * paideia-os shell: 0xFFFFECD/ECE/ED8..EDF (large)
#   * paideia-os mv: 0xFFFFEBC/EBD (large)
#   * paideia-os kernel Pipeline: 0xFFFFEC40..0xFFFFEC42 (large)
#   * kernel drivers: 0xFFFFFC_/FFFFFD_ clusters (large, disjoint)
#
# Grep confirmation at landing time:
